#, no-c-format
msgid "Festival"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:2101
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"American English, British, Spanish, German, Finnish, Czech, Polish, Russian, "
"Italian, French Canadian, Kiswahili, Zulu, and Ibibio"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:2106
#, no-c-format
msgid "Festival Lite (flite)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:2107 index.docbook:2122
#, no-c-format
msgid "English"
msgstr "Anglés"

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:2111
#, no-c-format
msgid "Hadifix (&mbrola; and txt2pho)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:2112
#, no-c-format
msgid "German, Hungarian"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:2116 index.docbook:2293
#, no-c-format
msgid "Epos"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:2117
#, no-c-format
msgid "Czech, Slovak"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:2121 index.docbook:2296
#, no-c-format
msgid "FreeTTS"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2130
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It also works with any synthesis engine that can be run from a command in a "
"&konsole;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2133
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The languages listed above may not be comprehensive or up-to-date. Check the "
"specifications for each engine for a complete list of supported languages. "
"Also check the <ulink url=\"http://accessibility.kde.org/developer/kttsd/"
"index.php\"> &ktts;</ulink> website for additional information that might "
"not have made it into this handbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2143
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&ktts; uses a flexible plugin architecture for speech synthesis engines. If "
"you want to enhance &ktts; to support another engine, contact the "
"development team."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2150
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"See <xref linkend=\"configuration\"/> for specific instructions for each of "
"these engines."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2158
#, no-c-format
msgid "At least one of the following audio subsystems:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2161
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kde; &arts; Soundsystem. &arts; is usually installed with &kde;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2162
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"ALSA (Advanced &Linux; Sound Architecture). ALSA is installed with most "
"&Linux; systems. (<ulink url=\"www.alsa-project.org\">www.alsa-project.org</"
"ulink>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2164
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"GStreamer version 0.8.7 or greater. <emphasis>Note</emphasis>: Be sure to "
"register your GStreamer plugins by running the <command>gst-register</"
"command> command prior to using GStreamer in &ktts;. (<ulink url=\"http://"
"gstreamer.freedesktop.org\"> http://gstreamer.freedesktop.org</ulink>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2169
#, no-c-format
msgid "aKode library. aKode is a decoder library that is part of &kde;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2173
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kde; project plans to drop &arts; starting in version 4."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2175
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Some users experience device contention with ALSA. If your system has this "
"problem, you will not be able to simultaneously play music while speaking. "
"&ktts; will also freeze if you pause a text job and then start another. See "
"the ALSA website (dmix) for possible solutions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2180
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As of July 2005, aKode does not support a true pause capability. When you "
"pause a text job in &ktts; it will finish speaking the current sentence."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2190
#, no-c-format
msgid "Optional components:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2196
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <command>sox</command> audio utility is needed for adjusting overall "
"speech speed, but not required. Debian users can install sox with the "
"command <command>apt-get install sox</command>. Sox is included on most "
"&Linux; distribution CDs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2203
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <command>xsltproc</command> utility is needed for SSML support and for "
"the &XML; Transformer filter, but not required. Debian users can install "
"xsltproc with the command <command>apt-get install xsltproc</command>."
msgstr ""

