#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2343
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using with Festival (Interactive)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2345
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Festival is one of the best free and open source TTS engines available. "
"Voice quality is generally good and there are quite a few languages and "
"voices supported. For many voices, you can control the volume, speed of the "
"generated speech, and pitch (tone) from &ktts;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2351
#, no-c-format
msgid "Synthesizer Name: <guilabel>Festival Interactive</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2353
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&URL;: <ulink url=\"http://www.cstr.ed.ac.uk/projects/festival/\"> http://"
"www.cstr.ed.ac.uk/projects/festival/</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2357
#, no-c-format
msgid "Debian Install Command: <userinput>apt-get install festival</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2359
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You will need to install at least one language. Follow the instructions that "
"come with Festival. If you will be speaking web pages, you must install the "
"<command>rab_diphone</command> (British Male) voice."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2366
#, no-c-format
msgid "Additional English festival voices are available from"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2368
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<ulink url=\"http://hts.ics.nitech.ac.jp/\">http://hts.ics.nitech.ac.jp/</"
"ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2371
#, no-c-format
msgid "Additional Spanish, English, and German voices are available from"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: index.docbook:2373
#, no-c-format
msgid "http://cslu.cse.ogi.edu/tts/download/"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2376
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You must compile an additional module for these voices, therefore, you must "
"have the Festival source code. The German voices have limited distribution."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2381
#, no-c-format
msgid "A Finnish male voice is available from"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2383
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<ulink url=\"http://www.ling.helsinki.fi/suopuhe/download/\"> http://www."
"ling.helsinki.fi/suopuhe/download/</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2387
#, no-c-format
msgid "A Polish male voice is available from"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2389
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<ulink url=\"http://www.artegence.com/download/voicexml/speech/"
"festival_polish_voice.tgz\"> http://www.artegence.com/download/voicexml/"
"speech/festival_polish_voice.tgz</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2393
#, no-c-format
msgid "A Russian male voice is available from"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: index.docbook:2395
#, no-c-format
msgid "http://nshmyrev.narod.ru/festival/festival.html"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2399
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You must have Festival 1.95 beta or later to use this voice. The voice is "
"still in early development. Untar to <filename>festival/lib/voices/russian/</"
"filename>. When you configure the Russian talker, the voice code is "
"<userinput>msu_ru_nsh_diphone</userinput>. Be sure to select an 8-bit "
"cryllic encoding, such as <userinput>KOI8-R</userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2405
#, no-c-format
msgid "Italian voices for Festival 1.95 beta are available at"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2407
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<ulink url=\"http://www.csrf.pd.cnr.it/TTS/It-FESTIVAL-download.htm\"> "
"http://www.csrf.pd.cnr.it/TTS/It-FESTIVAL-download.htm</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2410
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you get CRC errors when you unzip, try downloading again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2412
#, no-c-format
msgid "Kiswahili, Zulu, and Ibibio voices for Festival 1.95 beta are available at"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2414
#, no-c-format
msgid "<ulink url=\"http://www.llsti.org/\">http://www.llsti.org/</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2416
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, the Hindi voice also available there will not work with "
"&ktts;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2419
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Commercial voices, including a French Canadian voice, can be purchased from "
"Cepstral, LLC at"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: index.docbook:2422
#, no-c-format
msgid "http://www.cepstral.com/"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2424
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The FAQ on their Support page has information about using their voices in "
"Festival."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2427
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Festival is typically included with &Linux; distributions. Check your distro "
"CDs to see if it is included."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2431
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When using the Polish, Hungarian, or Czech languages, be sure the "
"<guilabel>Encoding</guilabel> option is set to <userinput>ISO 8859-2</"
"userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2434
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When using the Russian voice, be sure the <guilabel>Encoding</guilabel> "
"option is set to an 8-bit cryllic encoding, such as <userinput>KOI8-R</"
"userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2443
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using Festival with &mbrola;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2445
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Festival can be used in combination with the &mbrola; synthesizer. In this "
"mode, Festival does the lexical analysis and &mbrola; produces the audio. "
"The &mbrola; binary and &mbrola; voice files can be downloaded from"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2449
#, no-c-format
msgid "<ulink url=\"http://festvox.org/mbrola/\">http://festvox.org/mbrola/</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2451
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Follow the instructions in the <filename>readme.txt</filename> that comes "
"with the download."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2454
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note that &mbrola; is not a complete Text-to-Speech system. &mbrola; "
"synthesizes speech from diphone files. You must have additional software "
"that can produce the diphones. When combined with Festival, Festival "
"produces the diphones needed by &mbrola;. <command>txt2pho</command> can "
"also be used to produce diphones from German text. See <xref linkend=\"using-"
"with-hadifix\"/> for more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2460
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are three methods of combining Festival with &mbrola;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2464
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"mbrola-wrappers\">&mbrola; Wrappers</link>. At the time of "
"writing this Handbook, this method is limited to English voices."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2467
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"ims-german-festival\">IMS German Festival</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2468
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"festival-czech\">Festival-Czech</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2475
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using Festival with &mbrola; Wrappers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2477
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this method, additional wrapper code is added to Festival to enable "
"speech synthesis using &mbrola; voice files. Note that the &mbrola; voice "
"files are <emphasis>not</emphasis> installed in the &mbrola; folder tree. "
"Instead, they are installed in the <filename>festival/lib/</filename> folder "
"tree. For instructions, see"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: index.docbook:2483
#, no-c-format
msgid "http://www.cstr.ed.ac.uk/projects/festival/mbrola.html"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2491
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using IMS German Festival"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2493
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"IMS German Festival is a modified version of Festival that uses German "
"&mbrola; voices. It works with either Festival version 1.4.1 or Festival 2.0 "
"(1.95beta). First install Festival and &mbrola;, if you have not already "
"done so. Next, download IMS German Festival, from"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2498
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<ulink url=\"http://www.ims.uni-stuttgart.de/phonetik/synthesis/"
"festival_opensource.html\"> http://www.ims.uni-stuttgart.de/phonetik/"
"synthesis/festival_opensource.html</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2502
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Follow the instructions in the <filename>README</filename> that comes with "
"the download. (Note, if using in combination with Festival 2.0, it is "
"<emphasis>not</emphasis> necessary to apply the <filename>fixes</filename> "
"tarball, but you must still rebuild festival.) Finally, add the following "
"lines to the <filename>festival/lib/siteinit.scm</filename> file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: index.docbook:2509
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(voice-location \"german_de1_os\" \"/usr/local/mbrola/de1\"\n"
"  \"German Female, IMS Festival de1\")\n"
"(voice-location \"german_de2_os\" \"/usr/local/mbrola/de2\"\n"
"  \"German Male, IMS Festival de2\")\n"
"(voice-location \"german_de3_os\" \"/usr/local/mbrola/de3\"\n"
"  \"German Female, IMS Festival de3\")"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2512 index.docbook:2564
#, no-c-format
msgid "just above the line that reads"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: index.docbook:2515 index.docbook:2567
#, no-c-format
msgid "(provide 'siteinit)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2518
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On some systems, the file you edit is <filename>/etc/festival.scm</"
"filename>. Only add the lines that correspond to the German voices you have "
"installed. Substitute the correct path for <userinput><replaceable>/usr/"
"local/mbrola/</replaceable></userinput>. Also note that (at the time of this "
"writing) IMS German Festival does not work with the de4, de5, or de6 German "
"voices."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2530
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using Festival-Czech"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2532
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This method uses some special code to enable speech synthesis using Festival "
"with an &mbrola; Czech voice. To install, first download and install "
"Festival and &mbrola;, and make sure both are working. Next, download "
"Festival-Czech from"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: index.docbook:2537
#, no-c-format
msgid "http://www.freebsoft.org/festival-czech"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2540
#, no-c-format
msgid "In the following procedures substitute the correct folder paths as needed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2543
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Untar the download to a suitable folder and make the lexicon. The Festival "
"executable must be in your <envar>PATH</envar>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: index.docbook:2548
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"cd /usr/local\n"
"tar xvfz festival-czech.tar.gz\n"
"cd festival-czech\n"
"make"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2551
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Download the <filename>cz2</filename> voice file from the &mbrola; website, "
"and unzip it in the &mbrola; folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: index.docbook:2555
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"cd /usr/local/mbrola\n"
"mkdir cz2\n"
"cd cz2\n"
"unzip cz2-001009.zip"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2558
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Add the following lines to the <filename>festival/lib/siteinit.scm</"
"filename> file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: index.docbook:2561
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(set! czech-lexicon-file \"/usr/local/festival-czech/czech-lexicon.out\")\n"
"(set! load-path (cons \"/usr/local/festival-czech\" load-path))\n"
"(require 'czech)\n"
"(set! czech-mbrola_database \"/usr/local/mbrola/cz2/cz2\")\n"
"(set! mbrola_progname \"/usr/local/mbrola/mbrola\")\n"
"(voice-location \"czech_mbrola_cz2\" \"/usr/local/mbrola/cz2\"\n"
"    \"Czech Male, MBROLA\")\n"
"(require 'czech-mbrola)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2570
#, no-c-format
msgid "On some systems, the file you edit is <filename>/etc/festival.scm</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2581
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using with Festival Lite (flite)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2583
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Festival Lite is a free open source engine that currently supports a limited "
"number of voices and languages. It is light weight, but sacrifices voice "
"quality somewhat. You cannot control the pitch, volume, or speed of this "
"engine from &ktts;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2589
#, no-c-format
msgid "Synthesizer Name: <guilabel>Festival Lite (flite)</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2591
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&URL;: <ulink url=\"http://www.speech.cs.cmu.edu/flite/index.html\"> http://"
"www.speech.cs.cmu.edu/flite/index.html</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2595
#, no-c-format
msgid "Debian Install Command: <userinput>apt-get install flite</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2597
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"flite is typically included with &Linux; distributions. Check your distro "
"CDs to see if it is included."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2600
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Build and install flite following the instructions in the <filename>README</"
"filename> that comes with it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2609
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using with Hadifix (&mbrola; and txt2pho)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2611
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Hadifix is a two-stage synthesis engine based on diphones. The "
"<command>txt2pho</command> utility converts text into diphones and the "
"&mbrola; engine synthesizes the diphones to sound. Voice quality is good, "
"but language support is currently somewhat limited. You can control the "
"voice, pitch, speed, and volume from <application>kttsmgr</application>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2618
#, no-c-format
msgid "Synthesizer Name: <guilabel>Hadifix</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2620
#, no-c-format
msgid "&URL;: see below"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2622 index.docbook:2705 index.docbook:2723
#, no-c-format
msgid "Debian Install Command: none"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2624
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you do not already have Hadifix installed, do this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2627
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Download &mbrola; binary from <ulink url=\"http://festvox.org/mbrola/"
"\">http://festvox.org/mbrola/</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2629
#, no-c-format
msgid "Install &mbrola; to <filename>/usr/local/mbrola</filename> folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2630
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Download at least one german language file from the &mbrola; site. Unzip to "
"the <filename>/usr/local/mbrola</filename> folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2632
#, no-c-format
msgid "Download txt2pho from"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2633
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<ulink url=\"http://www.ikp.uni-bonn.de/dt/forsch/phonetik/hadifix/"
"HADIFIXforMBROLA.html\"> http://www.ikp.uni-bonn.de/dt/forsch/phonetik/"
"hadifix/HADIFIXforMBROLA.html</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2637
#, no-c-format
msgid "Unzip txt2pho to <filename>/usr/local/txt2pho</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2638
#, no-c-format
msgid "Edit <command>txt2phorc</command> file, putting correct data paths in."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2639
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Either copy <command>txt2phorc</command> to <filename>~/.txt2phorc</"
"filename> or to <filename>/etc/txt2pho</filename>. Note that you drop the "
"\"rc\" in file name."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2641
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In <application>kttsmgr</application>, choose the German language "
"(<guilabel>de</guilabel>), and add <guilabel>Hadifix</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2643
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the <guilabel>Configure Talker</guilabel> screen, configure a voice and "
"the paths to &mbrola; and txt2pho."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2645
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click the <guibutton>Test</guibutton> button to test."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2648
#, no-c-format
msgid "A Hungarian implementation for &mbrola; and txt2pho is available at"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2650
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<ulink url=\"http://tkltrans.sourceforge.net/\">http://tkltrans.sourceforge."
"net/</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2660
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using with Epos"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2662
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Epos is a free Czeck and Slovak open source engine. It is light weight, but "
"sacrifices voice quality somewhat. You cannot control the volume of this "
"engine from &ktts;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2667
#, no-c-format
msgid "Synthesizer Name: <guilabel>Epos TTS Synthesis System</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2669
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&URL;: <ulink url=\"http://epos.ure.cas.cz/\"> http://epos.ure.cas.cz/</"
"ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2673
#, no-c-format
msgid "Debian Install Command: <userinput>apt-get install epos</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2675
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Start <application>kttsmgr</application>. On the <guilabel>Talkers</"
"guilabel> tab, click the <guibutton>Add</guibutton> button. Choose Czeck or "
"Slovak language and <guilabel>Epos TTS Synthesis System</guilabel>. If the "
"epos server executable and client are not in your <envar>PATH</envar>, "
"specify the paths to these executables in the <guilabel>Configure Talker</"
"guilabel> screen. The options boxes permit you to pass additional options to "
"the server and client. In a &konsole;, type <userinput>epos -h</userinput> "
"or <userinput>say -h</userinput> for information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2691
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using with FreeTTS"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2693
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"FreeTTS is a free open source speech engine written in &Java;, which means "
"that you must have the &Java; Virtual Machine software installed on your "
"system to use it. It currently has limited voice and language support. You "
"cannot control the pitch, volume, or speed of this engine from &ktts;."
msgstr ""

